Link: https://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/20191101141009.15581-4-chris@chris-wilson.co.uk

Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from the premature shutdown of the rc6 feature during the `i915_gem_resume()` function, which is called during the preparation phase for all suspend paths. This behavior is incorrect because rc6 should only be shut down for certain suspend states (specifically S3+), leading to potential issues with hardware access to memory when the device is in a low power state (S0).

Here is the patch:

 void i915_gem_suspend(struct drm_i915_private *i915)
 {
 	GEM_TRACE("\n");

